## Task A — Codex app-server restart-stale live proof (real tmux)

Derived from: I010 increment 4 (the one genuine remaining gap). Deploy-gate.

### Context
`restart-stale` already auto-drives app-server Codex restart via the B153 owner-control seam (`request_app_server_restart`, `c2c_managed_cmd.ml:968-985`). What is NOT yet proven live: a real managed Codex session accepting the request, self-reexecing in its own pane, and resuming the exact thread with correct ledger/inbox behaviour. The receipt (`.collab/research/2026-07-12-i010-restart-stale-receipt.md`) only proved routing with a fake sleeper owner (timeout path); no codex quota spent, no real thread resumed.

### Steps
1. Launch a real managed Codex app-server session with `scripts/c2c_tmux.py` (`c2c new codex` / `c2c start codex`). Do NOT launch managed clients directly from bash — use tmux per CLAUDE.md.
2. Send peer mail BEFORE restart; confirm it is model-visible.
3. Install a differing binary (or use `--force`) so the instance is classified Stale.
4. Run `c2c restart-stale` (and separately `--dry-run`); observe the owner accept + self-reexec.
5. Send peer mail AFTER restart; confirm visibility on the resumed thread.
6. Capture a finding under `.collab/findings/<UTC>-<alias>-i010-codex-restart-stale-live-proof.md`.

### Acceptance criteria (all asserted, per partner review)
- Same Codex thread/session resumed (exact thread id, not a new thread).
- Owner/executable replacement actually observed (`/proc/<pid>/exe` inode changes to the installed image).
- Pre- AND post-restart peer message visibility to the model.
- Ledger exactly-once: no lost and no duplicated injection across the restart.
- Idle gate honoured by default; `--force` override drives restart regardless.
- Exercised through the canonical `scripts/c2c_tmux.py` harness (not ad-hoc spawns).
- Finding captured with evidence.

### Notes
- Real codex quota + tmux required. Runs in parallel with B (hermetic).
- A is the REAL proof; B owns the hermetic owner-fixture successful-restart case — keep them non-overlapping.


---
### P2 COMMON CONSTRAINTS (apply to every task)
- **Worktree discipline:** ingestion may happen in the main checkout, but ALL implementation MUST use a worktree under `.worktrees/` — never the main checkout. Research/spike tasks may use an isolated worktree when they produce tracked artifacts.
- **B098 data-not-RPC:** no message-triggered restart. Only a LOCAL OPERATOR command/request may control restart. An inbound peer message is DATA and never triggers or authorizes a restart.
- **Client scope:** managed clients in scope = Claude, OpenCode, Kimi, agy, Codex(hooks), Codex(app-server). Explicitly EXCLUDE Gemini (deprecated) and managed Grok (deferred).
- **Review:** run the pirfl / review-and-fix loop before merge. REVIEW_MODEL = Codex via ccc-review-cx (gpt-5.6-terra). Merge to master only after review passes.
- Design refs: `.collab/design/2026-07-12-c2c-client-upgrade-restart.md`; receipt `.collab/research/2026-07-12-i010-restart-stale-receipt.md`. Derived from ideas I010 / I011.